        <mxCell id="gOm3HKEUmkTU8l090uUw-1" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Rule of Reason become majority &amp;amp; other distinctions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Continental T.V., Inc. v. GTE Sylvania Inc&lt;/i&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Sylvania’s national television market share had fallen to approximately 1–2%. To strengthen its position, it replaced its broad distribution system with a smaller group of selected retailers. Each franchised retailer could sell Sylvania televisions only from approved locations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Continental was a successful Sylvania retailer. After Sylvania authorized another nearby retailer and refused Continental permission to open a Sacramento location, their relationship deteriorated. Sylvania eventually terminated Continental’s franchises. Continental claimed Sylvania’s location restriction violated § 1 of the Sherman Act.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;A jury found a violation under the Supreme Court’s earlier decision in Schwinn and awarded damages. The Ninth Circuit reversed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Schwinnn - overturned, tittle shifts - per se, can&#39;t partially pass a title&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Tittle stays - RoR because&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Schwann does apply &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="330" width="460" x="-3650" y="808" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gOm3HKEUmkTU8l090uUw-3" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Rule of Reason Become Majority&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Continental T.V., Inc. v. GTE Sylvania Inc&lt;/i&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Instead of assuming a per se rule, rule of reason should be the go to.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Because we are turning to economic evidence, using the pro - competitive effects&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="130" width="380" x="-3990" y="1230" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
