          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gOm3HKEUmkTU8l090uUw-5" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;JJ&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Continental T.V., Inc. v. GTE Sylvania Inc&lt;/i&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Justice Powell emphasized that vertical restrictions can have two competing effects:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;1. They reduce intrabrand competition by limiting competition among retailers selling the manufacturer’s brand.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;2. They can increase interbrand competition by helping the manufacturer compete more effectively against other brands.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="210" width="380" x="-4390" y="850" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gOm3HKEUmkTU8l090uUw-7" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;JJ&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Continental T.V., Inc. v. GTE Sylvania Inc&lt;/i&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;The Court identified several possible efficiencies:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Persuading competent retailers to carry a new or struggling brand.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Encouraging retailers to advertise and promote the product.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Encouraging service, repair facilities, demonstrations, trained employees, and other customer services.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Protecting product quality and the manufacturer’s reputation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Preventing free riding.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Interbrand - &amp;nbsp;cross brand - between two brands is more important&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Intrabrand - Same brand - retailers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="210" width="380" x="-4675" y="1138" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gOm3HKEUmkTU8l090uUw-9" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Vertical Non-price Restraint&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Continental T.V., Inc. v. GTE Sylvania Inc&lt;/i&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Explains why in this case the restraint on competition but doesn&#39;t say when it would be unlawful. Carves out an exception without any tie back to the main rule, making Vertical non-price restraints an exception?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Creates distinction between vertical vs horizontal and non - price vs. price.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="180" width="330" x="-3730" y="1370" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gOm3HKEUmkTU8l090uUw-29" edge="1" parent="1" source="gOm3HKEUmkTU8l090uUw-12" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="gOm3HKEUmkTU8l090uUw-28" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gOm3HKEUmkTU8l090uUw-12" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Free - Riding&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Continental T.V., Inc. v. GTE Sylvania Inc&lt;/i&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(1) one retailer pays to provide demonstrations, or customer service&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(2) but consumer obtains information and then purchases from a discount retailer&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(3) repeatedly&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Then full-service retailers may stop offering services, and from of territorial or location restrictions is allowed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="180" width="460" x="-3375" y="1205" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gOm3HKEUmkTU8l090uUw-24" edge="1" parent="1" source="gOm3HKEUmkTU8l090uUw-18" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="gOm3HKEUmkTU8l090uUw-23" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gOm3HKEUmkTU8l090uUw-27" edge="1" parent="1" source="gOm3HKEUmkTU8l090uUw-18" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;" target="gOm3HKEUmkTU8l090uUw-25">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gOm3HKEUmkTU8l090uUw-18" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Rule of Reason become majority &amp;amp; Resale Price Maintenance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Leegin Creative Leather Products, Inc. v. PSKS, Inc.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Leegin manufactured Brighton leather goods and sold primarily through small boutiques. It believed these retailers provided better service and a more distinctive shopping experience than large discount stores.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Leegin adopted a policy refusing to sell to retailers that discounted Brighton goods below suggested prices. It later created the “Heart Store” program, under which participating retailers pledged to follow suggested prices.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;PSKS operated Kay’s Kloset, which sold Brighton products and derived a substantial portion of its profits from them. When Kay’s Kloset discounted the entire Brighton line by 20%, Leegin asked it to stop. After it refused, Leegin stopped supplying the store.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;PSKS sued, alleging an agreement to fix minimum resale prices. Under Dr. Miles, minimum RPM was per se unlawful, so the trial court excluded Leegin’s evidence of procompetitive benefits. The jury found for PSKS, and the trebled judgment was approximately $4 million.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Holding&lt;/b&gt;:&amp;nbsp;minimum-price agreements must be evaluated under the rule of reason, not per se.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;retailers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Same brand restraints allows for cross brand competition&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="342" width="550" x="-2740" y="808" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gOm3HKEUmkTU8l090uUw-23" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Both procompetitive and anticompetitive effects&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Leegin Creative Leather Products, Inc. v. PSKS, Inc.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;procompetitive benefits include:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Preventing discount retailers from free riding on full-service retailers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Giving retailers sufficient margins to provide promotion and service.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Allowing retailers to compete through service rather than price.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Encouraging retailers to invest in introducing new brands.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Offering consumers different combinations of price and service.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Avoiding less efficient alternatives such as complete vertical integration or exclusive territories.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Anticompetitive possibilities recognized by the majority&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;The Court did not treat RPM as harmless. It explained that RPM may:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Facilitate a cartel among manufacturers by making discounting easier to detect.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Facilitate a retailer cartel when dealers pressure manufacturers to impose price floors.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Protect a dominant, inefficient retailer from innovative discount competitors.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- Allow a powerful manufacturer to reward retailers for excluding smaller rivals or new entrants.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="300" width="500" x="-2890" y="1190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gOm3HKEUmkTU8l090uUw-25" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Why RoR and not Per Se&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Leegin Creative Leather Products, Inc. v. PSKS, Inc.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;RPM can sometimes harm competition but can also promote competition.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(1) how widespread is RPM? if it&#39;s all manufacturers in a market (handbags) then could be manufacturer cartel, but if not then it&#39;s just vertical chain vs other vertical chain.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(2) who initiated? If manufacturer then just trying to control product price and be &quot;competitive&quot; but if retailer, then more suspicious of retailer trying to make a cartel via manufacturer&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(3) Possession of market power. Can they raise or lower prices without loosing too much business.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="250" width="500" x="-2360" y="1210" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gOm3HKEUmkTU8l090uUw-28" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Free - Riding&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Continental T.V., Inc. v. GTE Sylvania Inc&lt;/i&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;if one retailer has nice explanation but another one&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="180" width="460" x="-3350" y="1530" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FrW_EGITsQOS-twJgtxD-4" edge="1" parent="1" source="FrW_EGITsQOS-twJgtxD-1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="FrW_EGITsQOS-twJgtxD-3" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FrW_EGITsQOS-twJgtxD-1" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Market definition - the relevant competitive market&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Market Share - the portion of the market that a corporation owns&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Market Power - &amp;nbsp;the ability to exercise power over a consumer&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="100" width="370" x="1880" y="100" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FrW_EGITsQOS-twJgtxD-6" edge="1" parent="1" source="FrW_EGITsQOS-twJgtxD-3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="FrW_EGITsQOS-twJgtxD-5" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FrW_EGITsQOS-twJgtxD-8" edge="1" parent="1" source="FrW_EGITsQOS-twJgtxD-3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="FrW_EGITsQOS-twJgtxD-7" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FrW_EGITsQOS-twJgtxD-3" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Market definition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Du pont&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Geographic definition + product definition&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="110" width="270" x="1700" y="280" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FrW_EGITsQOS-twJgtxD-5" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Geographic definition&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="80" width="260" x="1510" y="440" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FrW_EGITsQOS-twJgtxD-7" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Product definition&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Du Pont&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Meta&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Scale (neither it the answer) : physically identical products &amp;lt;--------------&amp;gt; Canonically possible substitute &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;[1] Cross Elasticity of Demand: Interchangeability by consumers for the same purpose&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;(includes price, 2 or 3 x is considered not interchangeable)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Du pont&lt;/i&gt;: Not cellophane, but all wrapping including grease paper, foil, etc. determined by high cross elastic of demand.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Cellophane fallacy - You can&#39;t measure the willingness to switch, if monopoly is already in power and individuals are switching away from high prices.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Meta&lt;/i&gt;: Personal social networking v social networking&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;HMT (hypothetical monopolist test) - if 5-10% price change would cause switch then in the same market&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Meta&lt;/i&gt;: measure 5-10% quality instead of price&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="300" width="610" x="1850" y="440" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
